  "hypothesis": "Integrating flattened contiguous dataset storage (C), 64-byte aligned OpenMP SIMD distance computation (B), and a binary max-heap with exact (distance, global index) tie-breaking (A) should reduce runtime while preserving reference semantics including edge cases where fewer than k points exist.",
  "notes": "The implementation flattens all group point data into contiguous xs/ys/labels arrays, computes squared distances in parallel using OpenMP SIMD with aligned clauses on posix_memalign-allocated buffers, and selects the k nearest neighbors via a max-heap keyed by (distance, original index). Placeholder -1 labels are retained when total points < k to match the reference behavior. All memory is freed before returning.",
